        "title": "A msute see in Kathmandu",
        "text": "We visited the temple and surroundings in October 2014.  It is a very important Shiva site and the most important Hindu shrine in Nepal.  The temple is surrounded by many buildings and of course, the shore of the Bagmati River where cremations take place. You pass by vendor stalls on your way towards the temple.  You may see many cows meandering about as well.  To visit the Pashupatinath Temple, we utilized Prem, a guide.  Highly recommended.  He has a unique perspective as he lived about the temple as a street child and provided very worthwhile explanations of all that you’ll see.  After being adopted by an American couple he furthered his education and earned a master’s degree.  Prem’s English is very good and a tour with him to visit the temple area is an unforgettable experience.  We concluded our tour by viewing, from some distance and across the river, various cremations.  Prem can be reached via telephone: +977-9849082363 or e-mail premthapa305@hotmail.com",
