      {
        "review_id": 236293102,
        "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r236293102-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html",
        "title": "shiva statue manifested as Shivalinga!!",
        "text": "The temple is very popular and famous in Hindus. The temple is located about 7 km from Kathmandu city. It is a temple worth to visit !!. It is one of the Panch Kedar kshetra. \n\nOne can do abhishekam of Lord Shiv in INR 1100/-.The temple is situated on the banks of River Vishnumati or Bagmati. In the temple complex, there are many other temple of God and Goddess.\n\nDon't miss the temple of Shakti (Maa Durga) known as Guhyeshwari devi, which is very near to Pashupatinath (less than 1.5 km) and which is one of the 51 divine shaktipeeth of Maa Durga.\n\nOne can purchase Shaligram, a holy stone from the market just outside the temple.\n\nIt is a must visit temple.\nCheap accommodation is not available nearby, it is available in kathmandu city.\n\nOther important Hindu Temple in and nearby Kathmandu :\n1) Dakshineshwar Kali\n2) Budha Nilkantha\n3) Changu Narayan (15+ km from city)\n4) Krishna Temple (Patan)\n5) Baglamukhi temple and nearby temples (Patan)\n6) Jagannath temple (Hanuman dhoka square) and nearby temples\n\nIf you want to visit these temple, you can cover them in max. 2 days.",
